.git
.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/data
**/dist
# Multi-GB intermediate training checkpoints/optimizer state -- never copied
# into the image, or the build context balloons to multiple GB / a slow or
# failing build. The final trained model (training/output/*/final/) IS now
# copied into the image by the Dockerfile (it's the team's own real model,
# not the generic pretrained one) -- Docker's .dockerignore negation cannot
# re-include a path whose PARENT directory is itself excluded, so this must
# stay scoped to just the checkpoints subdirectory, not the whole
# training/output tree, or the Dockerfile's COPY of final/ would silently
# fail to find its source.
training/output/*/checkpoints
**/*.log
**/*.err
test.eml
.env
.env.*
# Mirrors .gitignore's secret-shaped entries: these are already excluded from
# git history, but .dockerignore is a separate control guarding the build
# CONTEXT -- without this, a local `docker build .` (a normal dev/CI action)
# would bake these into an image layer, extractable indefinitely from any
# image that's ever pushed anywhere, regardless of git state.
backend/gmail_oauth_client.json
backend/gmail_token.json
backend/gmail_watch_state.json
backend/gmail_oauth_setup.log
backend/serve_local.py
